@host = http://localhost:5226

### ============================================================
### Ask-My-Books — end-to-end demo of all 5 required endpoints
### Run top to bottom. Requests that need an id from an earlier
### response have a placeholder you can paste into.
### ============================================================


### 1) POST /books — create (Postgres + embed + index in Qdrant) -> 201
POST {{host}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Project Hail Mary",
  "author": "Andy Weir",
  "genre": "Science Fiction",
  "status": "Finished",
  "notes": "A lone astronaut wakes up with amnesia on a mission to save Earth from a solar dimming event. Loved the science-heavy problem solving and the unlikely friendship with Rocky.",
  "rating": 5,
  "finishedOn": "2025-03-14"
}


### 1b) A second book, different genre — gives Ask something to disambiguate
POST {{host}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Atomic Habits",
  "author": "James Clear",
  "genre": "Self-Help",
  "status": "Finished",
  "notes": "Practical framework for building good habits and breaking bad ones, centered on tiny 1% improvements and identity-based change.",
  "rating": 4,
  "finishedOn": "2024-11-02"
}


### 1c) A wishlist book (rating/finishedOn not allowed for this status)
POST {{host}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Thinking, Fast and Slow",
  "author": "Daniel Kahneman",
  "genre": "Psychology",
  "status": "Wishlist",
  "notes": "About the two systems driving how we think: fast intuition versus slow deliberate reasoning, and the biases that come from relying on the wrong one."
}


### ============================================================


### 2) GET /books — list everything from Postgres -> 200
GET {{host}}/books


### 2b) GET /books — filter by status
GET {{host}}/books?status=Finished


### 2c) GET /books — filter by author
GET {{host}}/books?author=Andy%20Weir


### ============================================================


### 4) POST /books/extract — messy text -> LLM -> validated record -> saved -> 201
POST {{host}}/books/extract
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "just finished dune by frank herbert last week, easily a 5/5. epic political sci-fi on the desert planet arrakis. finished it on 2025-06-20."
}


### 4b) Extract from a vaguer note — the model should infer sensible defaults
POST {{host}}/books/extract
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "adding klara and the sun by kazuo ishiguro to my to-read pile, heard great things"
}


### ============================================================


### 5) POST /ask — semantic Q&A grounded in the indexed books -> 200
### Worded completely differently from any note above: this proves
### semantic search, not keyword matching.
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Which book did I read about someone stranded in space trying to save humanity?"
}


### 5b) Another semantic query, no shared vocabulary with the notes
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Any books that helped me build better daily routines?"
}


### 5c) Out-of-scope question -> honest "I don't have that", never a guess
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "What is my favorite pizza topping?"
}


### ============================================================


### 3) DELETE /books/{id} — removes from Postgres AND Qdrant -> 204
### Paste a real id from one of the responses above.
DELETE {{host}}/books/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


### 3b) Deleting the same id again -> 404 (already gone)
DELETE {{host}}/books/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


### ============================================================
### Error handling — none of these should ever crash the API
### ============================================================


### Bad LLM output: nothing extractable as a book -> 400
POST {{host}}/books/extract
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "asdkjaslkdj random gibberish text with no book information whatsoever"
}


### Invalid status -> 400
POST {{host}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bad Status Example",
  "author": "Someone",
  "genre": "Test",
  "status": "NotARealStatus",
  "notes": ""
}


### Rating without Finished status -> 400 (domain rule)
POST {{host}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bad Rating Example",
  "author": "Someone",
  "genre": "Test",
  "status": "Reading",
  "notes": "",
  "rating": 5
}


### Empty question -> 400
POST {{host}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": ""
}
